From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:23:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [zlib][x86] Check CPU and OS support before AVX-512
 CRC-32

With CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL (CMake ENABLE_SIMD_AVX512), the AVX-512
CRC-32 kernel is enabled by _xgetbv(0) & 0x40 alone:

- XGETBV faults unless the CPU has XSAVE and the OS enabled OSXSAVE.
- CPUID is never checked for AVX-512F or VPCLMULQDQ, so AVX-512 CPUs
  without VPCLMULQDQ (e.g. Skylake-X) fault in the kernel.
- XCR0 bit 6 alone does not mean the XMM, YMM and opmask state is
  enabled.

Check XSAVE/OSXSAVE before XGETBV, then AVX-512F, VPCLMULQDQ and XCR0
0xe6. Also zero the upper lanes of the initial CRC vector; those of
_mm512_castsi128_si512 are undefined. GN builds do not define
CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL and are unchanged.

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
